CORE
array_partial_writes.sv
--top main --bound 2
^\[main\.p_A\] .*: PROVED up to bound 2$
^\[main\.p_B\] .*: PROVED up to bound 2$
^\[main\.p_C\] .*: PROVED up to bound 2$
^\[main\.p_E\] .*: PROVED up to bound 2$
^\[main\.p_F\] .*: PROVED up to bound 2$
^\[main\.p_G\] .*: PROVED up to bound 2$
^\[main\.r_A\] .*: REFUTED$
^\[main\.r_C\] .*: REFUTED$
^\[main\.r_G\] .*: REFUTED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
--
Partial writes into memory words at runtime addresses, compared with a
reference memory written with one whole word per cycle: byte enables and an
overlapping write (the later wins), guarded bit writes, writes at two
addresses that may be equal, blocking writes with reads of the written word,
nonblocking writes with a read of the old word, read-modify-write of bits.
